\engtitle{.. Dehastha Devata Chakra Stotram ..}##
\itxtitle{.. dehasthadevatAchakrastotram ..}##\endtitles ##
deho devAlayaH proktaH svAtmA devaH sanAtanaH |
tyajedaj~nAnanirmAlyaM so.ahaM bhAvena pUjayet || 1||
asurasuravR^indavanditamabhimatavaravitaraNe niratam |
darshanashatAgryapUjyaM prANatanuM gaNapatiM vande || 2||
varavIrayoginIgaNasiddhAvalipUjitA~Nghriyugalam |
apahR^itavinayijanArtiM vaTukamapAnAbhidhaM vande || 3||
yaddhIbalena vishvaM bhaktAnAM shivapathaM bhAti |
tamahamavadhAnarUpaM sadgurumamalaM sadA vande || 4||
AtmIyaviShayabhogairindriyadevyaH sadA hR^idambhoje |
abhipUjayanti yaM taM chinmayamAnandabhairavaM vande || 5||
udayAvabhAsacharvaNalIlAM vishvasya yA karotyanisham |
AnandabhairavIM tAM vimarsharUpAmahaM vande || 6||
archayati bhairavaM yA nishchayakusumaiH sureshapatrasthA |
praNamAmi buddhirUpAM brahmANIM tAmahaM satatam || 7||
kurute bhairavapUjAmanaladalasthA.abhimAnakusumairyA |
nityamaha~NkR^itirUpAM vande tAM shAmbhavImambAm || 8||
vidadhAti bhairavArchAM dakShiNadalagA viSheshakusumairyA | (vikalpakusumairyA)
nityaM manaHsvarUpAM kaumArIM tAmahaM vande || 9||
nairR^itadalagA bhairavamarchayate shabdakusumairyA |
praNamAmi shrutirUpAM nityaM tAM vaiShNavIM shaktim || 10|| (shabdarUpAm)

pashchimadigdalasaMsthA hR^idayaharaiH sparshakusumairyA |
toShayati bhairavaM tAM tvagrUpadharAM namAmi vArAhIm || 11||
varatararUpavisheShairmArutadigdalaniShaNNadehA yA |
pUjayati bhairavaM tAmindrANIM dR^iktanuM vande || 12||
dhanapatikisalayanilayA yA nityaM vividhaShaDrasAhAraiH |
pUjayati bhairavaM tAM jihvAbhikhyAM namAmi chAmuNDAm || 13||
IshadalasthA bhairavamarchayate parimalairvichitrairyA
praNamAmi sarvadA tAM ghrANAbhikhyAM mahAlakShmIm || 14||
ShaDdarshaneShu pUjyaM ShaDtriMshattattvasaMvalitam |
AtmAbhikhyaM satataM kShetrapatiM siddhidaM vande || 15||
saMsphuradanubhavasAraM sarvAntaH satatasannihitam |
naumi sadoditamitthaM nijadehagadevatAchakram || 16||

iti shrIabhinavaguptapAdAchAryakR^itaM dehasthadevatAchakrastotraM sampUrNam ||

##
There is a little variation between prints in relation to
verse 1 and reversed order of shlokas 4-5.

Encoded and proofread by Ruma Dewan

